WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:10.625
After the incident with Buttercup, Dan tried to behave for a few days.

2
00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:15.989
But it wasn't long before he went back to his old ways.

3
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:21.610
"Let's have some fun," he said one night to Nat.

4
00:00:21.611 --> 00:00:27.933
He pulled a bottle of root beer, a small cake, and some cards from under his bed.

5
00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:34.689
Nat's eyes widened. "Where did you get that food?" he asked.

6
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:39.711
"It was sitting in the kitchen all day," Dan explained with a shrug.

7
00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:44.348
"Asia always tells me I can help myself to snacks.

8
00:00:44.349 --> 00:00:52.937
Besides, nobody is around—Mr. Bauer's away, and Mrs. Bauer is busy with Teddy, who's sick or something.

9
00:00:52.938 --> 00:00:56.506
Don't you want to learn how to play poker?"

10
00:00:56.507 --> 00:01:01.030
Tempted by the adventure, Nat nodded.

11
00:01:01.031 --> 00:01:07.164
"Well, we need another player, so go get Tommy, and bring a candle for more light."

12
00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:11.687
"I'll bring Demi too," said Nat, who shared a room with Demi.

13
00:01:11.688 --> 00:01:19.356
"No, he'll just tell on us or try to stop us. Besides, he's probably asleep."

14
00:01:19.357 --> 00:01:26.944
Nat ran off and returned with a candle and Tommy, who was always ready for fun.

15
00:01:26.945 --> 00:01:37.477
"First we'll eat, and then we'll play cards for money," Dan said as he passed the root beer and cake around.

16
00:01:37.478 --> 00:01:40.255
"That's what real men do."

17
00:01:40.256 --> 00:01:44.814
"I wish we didn't have to be so quiet," Tommy said softly.

18
00:01:44.815 --> 00:01:48.807
"But we don't want Silas to hear us."

19
00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:57.734
Silas managed the property for Mr. Bauer, and his room was right next door.

20
00:01:57.735 --> 00:02:04.294
Suddenly a voice in the hall wailed, "I can't find Nat!"

21
00:02:04.295 --> 00:02:09.055
Then the boys heard the patter of bare feet.

22
00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:15.904
"It's Demi, and he's gone to get Mrs. Bauer," Dan cried, whisking everything out of sight.

23
00:02:15.905 --> 00:02:19.901
"Get in bed, everyone!"

24
00:02:19.902 --> 00:02:23.189
Tommy and Nat flew to their rooms.

25
00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:30.590
Hearing Demi's voice again, Nat quickly blew out his candle and tossed it under his bed.

26
00:02:30.591 --> 00:02:37.038
When Demi arrived with Jo a few seconds later, Nat was pretending to be asleep.

27
00:02:37.039 --> 00:02:44.027
But Jo wasn't fooled. "What mischief are you up to?"

28
00:02:44.028 --> 00:02:49.036
"What?" Nat said sleepily.

29
00:02:49.037 --> 00:02:55.271
"I only ran into Dan's room for a minute . . . I'm so sleepy . . . "

30
00:02:55.272 --> 00:03:01.260
Jo gave up and returned to Teddy, and Nat was soon asleep for real.

31
00:03:01.261 --> 00:03:08.806
Little did he realize what was happening under his bed—the candle was not out!

32
00:03:08.807 --> 00:03:13.727
Meanwhile Silas had awakened because he smelled something burning.

33
00:03:13.728 --> 00:03:20.123
Poking his head into the hall, he saw smoke coming from Nat and Demi's room.

34
00:03:20.124 --> 00:03:27.020
"Fire! Fire!" Silas cried, running to rescue the sleeping boys.

35
00:03:27.021 --> 00:03:32.281
Nat's bed was on fire, and the flames were licking the curtains.

36
00:03:32.282 --> 00:03:39.931
By the time Silas had pulled Nat and Demi to safety, Jo was on the scene.

37
00:03:39.932 --> 00:03:43.901
"Dan! Jack! Bring water from the bathroom!

38
00:03:43.902 --> 00:03:46.077
Tommy, get more buckets from the kitchen!

39
00:03:46.078 --> 00:03:49.552
Daisy, tell Asia I need her right now!

40
00:03:49.553 --> 00:03:54.220
Rob, stay out of the way!" The

41
00:03:54.221 --> 00:03:58.901
fire was quickly under control. Demi

42
00:03:58.902 --> 00:04:06.356
was more frightened than hurt, but Nat had a painful burn on his arm. When

43
00:04:06.357 --> 00:04:12.168
Mr. Bauer returned the next day, the boys gathered around him. Nat

44
00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:22.396
and Tommy immediately apologized for lying about the poker game, and the danger they'd caused, but Dan remained defiant. "You

45
00:04:22.397 --> 00:04:27.633
know I hate gambling, Dan," the professor said with a frown. "And

46
00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:31.449
you took a treat that Asia had left for Silas! Worst

47
00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.957
of all, you've involved the other boys in your misdeeds." "I

48
00:04:35.958 --> 00:04:40.340
didn't know it was a treat for Silas," Dan snapped. "Besides,

49
00:04:40.341 --> 00:04:43.702
not much harm was done." "Not

50
00:04:43.703 --> 00:04:49.606
much harm?" The professor raised his eyebrows in surprise. "The

51
00:04:49.607 --> 00:04:58.663
burn on Nat's arm is a terrible punishment, and Tommy is truly sorry. But you, Dan, have not even apologized. We've

52
00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:06.091
forgiven you many times, but it has done no good—you're still setting a bad example. So

53
00:05:06.092 --> 00:05:10.596
say good-bye to everyone, and pack up your things." "Where's

54
00:05:10.597 --> 00:05:14.146
he going?" Nat cried. "To

55
00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:20.695
Mr. Page's school in the country because Mr. Page has straightened out many troubled boys." "Will

56
00:05:20.696 --> 00:05:24.722
he ever come back?" Demi asked. "I

57
00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:31.304
hope so, but that's up to Dan himself," Mr. Bauer said. After

58
00:05:31.305 --> 00:05:37.226
Mr. Bauer left the room, the boys were full of questions for Dan. "Will

59
00:05:37.227 --> 00:05:41.594
you like it at Mr. Page's school?" Jack asked. "I

60
00:05:41.595 --> 00:05:45.519
won't stay if I don't," Dan replied. "Where

61
00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.858
would you go?" Nat asked. "Maybe

62
00:05:48.859 --> 00:05:57.136
I'll go to sea or out to California," Dan said with a reckless air that startled the boys. "Oh,

63
00:05:57.137 --> 00:06:03.530
don't do that! Stay with Mr. Page awhile and then come back here," Nat pleaded. "I'm

64
00:06:03.531 --> 00:06:15.932
never coming back here !" Dan stormed upstairs to pack his things, every one of which Mr. Bauer had given him.

65
00:06:15.933 --> 00:06:24.257
When it was time to leave, Jo came outside, looking so sad that Dan felt remorseful.

66
00:06:24.258 --> 00:06:28.433
"May I go in to say good-bye to Teddy?" he asked.

67
00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:37.221
"Yes, he'll miss his Danny very much," Jo said, and followed him upstairs.

68
00:06:37.222 --> 00:06:43.866
While Dan was bending over Teddy's bed, he heard Jo talking to her husband.

69
00:06:43.867 --> 00:06:50.064
"Can't we give him another chance—he's the only boy we've ever failed with."

70
00:06:50.065 --> 00:06:54.080
But Mr. Bauer's mind was firmly made up.

71
00:06:54.081 --> 00:07:01.045
Dan wanted to ask for one more chance, but his pride wouldn't allow him.

72
00:07:01.046 --> 00:07:09.765
So, with a stony look on his face, he climbed into the wagon.

73
00:07:09.766 --> 00:07:15.972
A few days later, Mr. Page sent a letter, saying Dan was doing well.

74
00:07:15.973 --> 00:07:22.573
But three weeks later, another letter arrived, and this one said that Dan had run away.

75
00:07:22.574 --> 00:07:29.666
Mr. Bauer sighed. "Perhaps I should have given him another chance."

76
00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:36.477
"Don't worry, Fritz," Jo said. "I'm sure he'll come back to us."

77
00:07:36.478 --> 00:07:42.616
But time passed, and Dan did not return.

